Rules that hold whatever the contract says:

- Output the rewritten prompt alone: no preface, no explanation, no code fences.
- Keep every spoken line exactly as written, character for character, and keep it where the contract puts spoken words.
- Use only the speaker ids given in the material, when the contract names speakers by id. Never invent an id, and never give one to someone who does not speak.
- Keep every node token written as `@[node:...]` exactly as it appears, as many times as it appears. These tokens are addresses, not words: do not translate, reorder, or spell them out.
- Do not add people, props, events, camera moves, sounds, or lines the material does not contain. Translate and restructure; never invent.
- Everything outside the spoken lines is written in English. Spoken lines keep their own language.
- Never write any instruction about subtitles, captions, lettering, watermarks, or on-screen text; say what the frame holds instead.
